"""Items part 4: the human's side of the items (game/human_items.cpp)

Run: set MUT_HARNESS=items, MUT_BAT=build_human.bat, MUT_DEFS=-DHUMAN_ITEMS_TEST, MUT_EXTRA_SRCS=ls3df/src/math/math.cpp,
MUT_EXTRA_INC=ls3df/src, then python _re/harness/mutrun.py _re/harness/items/mutations/mutate_items4.py WORK [JOBS].
Needs ITEMS_SAV and EQUIPMENT_SAVE (see build.bat). Labels: T + line.
Generated by _re/harness/shots/gen_mutations.py (lines unique in the file).

Result (2026-11-10): 260 mutants; 215 killed, 29 not building, 16 survived:
- equivalent: T 148 cmp (CollectInContainer's result: CollectItems ignores it), T 184 / 191 del (the containers' max
  weight is 100 already), T 396 num (-1 -> -2: still "not found"), T 403 cmp / num (a found slot is never empty),
  T 498 num (uid -2 only tells the second move of a displaced new item, from no actor to no actor: no one to tell),
  T 791 num (the source container of an item from no actor), T 862 cmp (the store's slot past the used ones is
  empty), T 900 del (the command's param2 is 0 already);
- leaks: T 218 cmp, T 219 / 220 del (Done not deleting the backpack's slot / the containers / the array);
- not observable here: T 662 arith, T 663 del (the debug output of a failed drop);
- unreachable: T 881 bool (a null controller is dereferenced before).
First run: 198 killed, 33 survived; added since (TestPart4Edges): Init on an object marked single-container, a
type only in the backpack's contents, the uid of CreateItemInStore, a belt holding only a sidearm, the moves with
the mission running (the equipment told, a locked container), a drop to temporary actor 0, hands weapons of
capacity 1 and 0, GetTeam's argument, a zone with actor id 0.
Checked against the original's asm: RequestThrowItem (0x005a2c50), DropAllItems' velocities and hands rule
(0x005a2fe0), CountAmmo (0x005a6c50), GetEquipmentState's order and the type 38 rule (0x005a8b50), ServerMoveItem's
lookup (0x005a2d50), ClearContainers (0x005a29c0).
"""
